    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Bogdan,<div><br></div><div>Which version of TitanCNA are you using? In v1.7.2, I have included a check for clusters that contain very few data points (i.e. cluster=2 solution only have a few data points for Z1). See <a href=\"https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/NEWS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/NEWS&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793235415315000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2aFmrVJfzBoVdIphW40sxQ\">https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/NEWS</a> for <span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">removeEmptyClusters()</span><br></div><div>Also, are you using a helper script for selecting your solutions? <a href=\"https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/scripts/R_scripts/selectSolution.R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/scripts/R_scripts/selectSolution.R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793235415315000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1S6XvBjW-MDIMffF_-25gv\">https://github.com/gavinha/TitanCNA/blob/master/scripts/R_scripts/selectSolution.R</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Based on the plots, numClusters=1 appears to be more accurate. It is possible that there are other chromosomes that support sub clonal events (numClusters=2) but from chr12 alone, it seems 1 cluster is correct. It is good that you are manually inspecting your results.</div><div>The reason cluster=2 is incorrect in this plot is because it has overfitted to a sub clonal (Z2) cluster and therefore very few data points are in Z1. If all the chromosomes look like this, that is, all chromosomes have most data points in Z2 and not Z1, then <span style=\"color:rgb(36,41,46);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre\">removeEmptyClusters() </span>should have corrected this solution. Of course, unless there is an abundance of noisy data in Z1 that avoids correction.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Gavin</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, September 14, 2018 at 1:12:49 AM UTC-7, Bogdan Tanasa wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:12pt\">Dear Gavin, and all, </span><div><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:12pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:black;font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:12pt\">if I may ask please for your suggestions  on the following :  given an ostesarcoma sample, based on\r\nSDbw Validity index, I shall select the results for the parameter \r\n2_NumClusters (the file is  &quot;chr12.2.numClusters.5.copyNumbers.TITAN.ALL_these_4figures.png&quot;)</span><div><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">However, given this result, I am somehow\r\nunclear, because a predicted DEL (in green) on the LRR plot does not display the typical BAF for a deletion.</span></font></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">In\r\n contrast, the prediction for this\r\nchromosome makes more sense shall we select 1_Numclusters (as shown in \r\nthe other file that &#39;ve attached : \r\nchr12.1.numClusters.5.copyNumbers.TITAN.ALL_these_4figures.png); however\r\n it is a higher SDbw Validity index for the run 1_Numclusters.</span></font></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n\r\n</span></font></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">i would appreciate any suggestion regarding\r\non how to interpret the data. Thank you, </span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\"><br></span></font></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"3\" face=\"Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,Apple Color Emoji,Segoe UI Emoji,NotoColorEmoji,Segoe UI Symbol,Android Emoji,EmojiSymbols\" color=\"black\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\" dir=\"ltr\">-- bo